      "text": "<think>\nFirst, I need to calculate the product of 99 and 99.\n\nI can use the formula for squaring a binomial: (a - b)\u00b2 = a\u00b2 - 2ab + b\u00b2.\n\nApplying this to 99, which is 100 - 1, I get:\n\n(100 - 1)\u00b2 = 100\u00b2 - 2(100)(1) + 1\u00b2 = 10,000 - 200 + 1 = 9,801.\n\nTherefore, the product of 99 and 99 is 9,801.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 99 and 99, we can use the formula for squaring a binomial:\n\n\\[\n(a - b)^2 = a^2 - 2ab + b^2\n\\]\n\nLet's apply this formula to \\(99\\), which can be expressed as \\(100 - 1\\):\n\n\\[\n99^2 = (100 - 1)^2\n\\]\n\nNow, expand the expression using the binomial formula:\n\n\\[\n(100 - 1)^2 = 100^2 - 2 \\times 100 \\times 1 + 1^2\n\\]\n\nCalculate each term:\n\n\\[\n100^2 = 10,000\n\\]\n\\[\n2 \\times 100 \\times 1 = 200\n\\]\n\\[\n1^2 = 1\n\\]\n\nNow, substitute these values back into the equation:\n\n\\[\n99^2 = 10,000 - 200 + 1 = 9,801\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{9,\\!801}\n\\]",
