      "text": "<think>\nFirst, I need to calculate the product of 99 and 81.\n\nI can use the distributive property to simplify the multiplication.\n\nI'll break down 99 into 100 minus 1 and 81 into 80 plus 1.\n\nSo, 99 \u00d7 81 becomes (100 - 1) \u00d7 (80 + 1).\n\nNext, I'll expand the expression using the distributive property:\n\n100 \u00d7 80 + 100 \u00d7 1 - 1 \u00d7 80 - 1 \u00d7 1.\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n100 \u00d7 80 = 8000\n\n100 \u00d7 1 = 100\n\n1 \u00d7 80 = 80\n\n1 \u00d7 1 = 1\n\nNow, I'll add all these results together:\n\n8000 + 100 - 80 - 1 = 8019.\n\nTherefore, the product of 99 and 81 is 8019.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 99 and 81, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Break Down the Numbers:**\n   \n   - **99** can be written as **100 - 1**.\n   - **81** can be written as **80 + 1**.\n\n2. **Apply the Distributive Property:**\n   \n   \\[\n   99 \\times 81 = (100 - 1) \\times (80 + 1)\n   \\]\n\n3. **Expand the Expression:**\n   \n   \\[\n   (100 - 1) \\times (80 + 1) = 100 \\times 80 + 100 \\times 1 - 1 \\times 80 - 1 \\times 1\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate Each Term:**\n   \n   \\[\n   100 \\times 80 = 8000\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   100 \\times 1 = 100\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   1 \\times 80 = 80\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   1 \\times 1 = 1\n   \\]\n\n5. **Add All the Results Together:**\n   \n   \\[\n   8000 + 100 - 80 - 1 = 8019\n   \\]\n\n6. **Final Answer:**\n   \n   \\[\n   \\boxed{8019}\n   \\]",
